Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ga36mb-jd9366: experiment E4, non-burst video with sync pulses

Experiment kernel of device-fixes 6.3 (D12, P-95 E4), never in the default image.

Burst mode (the default and the vendor lcd_dsi_if = 2) sends each line as one fast
packet and leaves the lanes in LP-11 for the rest of the line: the panel has to
place the line from its own timing after every HS entry. Non-burst video with sync
pulses keeps the link in HS for the whole line, with the HSync start and end
packets and blanking packets at the pixel rate (sun6i_mipi_dsi builds them when
MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST is off; the PinePhone panel runs this way on the same
DSI block). Same clock and totals. If the ghost image shifted down is the panel
losing the line position when hot, explicit sync pulses should keep it.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c
@@ -447,9 +447,10 @@
 	mipi_dsi_set_drvdata(dsi, ctx);
 	dsi->lanes = 2;
 	dsi->format = MIPI_DSI_FMT_RGB888;
-	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST |
+	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_SYNC_PULSE |
 			  MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM | MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS;
 	ctx->panel.prepare_prev_first = true;
+	dev_info(dev, "experiment kernel e4-nonburst: non-burst video with sync pulses\n");
 
 	ret = jd9366_check_bus(ctx, dsi);
 	if (ret < 0) {
